# Project Rules for AI Agents

## Project Overview
This is an n8n automation project that uses the n8n MCP server to create workflows programmatically.

## Code Standards
- Use TypeScript for all new code
- Follow n8n node naming conventions
- Always validate workflows before deployment
- Use meaningful variable names

## Workflow Development Guidelines
1. Always check for existing templates before creating new workflows
2. Use parallel tool execution for better performance
3. Validate all node configurations
4. Never trust default parameter values
5. Add comprehensive error handling

## Common Patterns
- Webhook → Process → Notify pattern for event-driven workflows
- Use IF nodes for conditional logic with proper branch connections
- Always include error handling nodes

## Testing Requirements
- Test all workflows with sample data before deployment
- Verify webhook endpoints are accessible
- Check all external API connections

## Documentation
- Document all workflow purposes in workflow descriptions
- Add comments to complex code nodes
- Include example payloads for webhook triggers
